Task: Redesign ONLY the BlueMind iOS AI/model selector popover.

The current implementation became too large/tall after the last modification and no longer feels polished.

I want to keep ALL existing functionality and options, but change the presentation and interaction.

This selector contains THREE independent settings:

1. BlueMind model / AI power
    * BlueMind 3.0
    * BlueMind 3.5
    * BlueMind 4.0
    * BlueMind 4.5
    * BlueMind 5.0
2. AI specialization / mode
    * General AI
    * Study AI
    * Research AI
    * Work AI
    * Writing AI
    * Coding AI
    * and any other existing modes already present in the code.
3. Thinking
    * existing Thinking option/state.

Do not remove or change the underlying logic of any of these settings.

⸻

MAIN PROBLEM

The current selector is too tall and feels like a large page/card.

I do NOT want it to expand almost to the full available screen just because there are many options.

Instead, make it a medium-height floating iOS popover.

It should be:

* clearly larger than a tiny dropdown;
* clearly smaller than a full-screen sheet;
* visually balanced;
* centered/aligned naturally below the current AI selector button;
* internally scrollable.

Think of the attached reference selector: a floating panel with a controlled maximum height, while its contents scroll inside.

⸻

FIXED / CONTROLLED POPOVER HEIGHT

Give the popover a responsive maximum height appropriate for the current iPhone viewport.

Do NOT calculate its height from the total number of options.

If all options do not fit:

the popover remains the same medium size and the CONTENT scrolls vertically inside it.

The outer popover itself should not keep becoming taller.

Avoid a hardcoded height that only works on one iPhone. Use available viewport/safe-area dimensions and clamp it to a sensible medium range.

⸻

INTERNAL SCROLL

Put the model list, AI modes, and Thinking section inside one smooth vertical scroll area.

The user should be able to scroll:

BlueMind Models
↓
AI Modes
↓
Thinking

